<blockquote>
<p>Celcius is literally the same thing as Kelvin +273.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yes, so including both is pointless. There is one important difference, K works with SI prefixes and derived units.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>°F, on the other hand, is based on illogical moon people units</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How is a sodium chloride solution any less logical than water?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the rest of the imperial system</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why is everyone always concerned with the Imperial system? The Imperial system is dead and buried for the most part and has been for half a century now. US Customary is what you should be worried about. Unlike most other US Customary units, degrees Fahrenheit <em>are metric</em>, though. They are base ten units derived from an empirical standard.</p>
