<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>I do have concerns about the quick dismissal of degrees Celsius as not a &quot;real SI unit&quot;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think it is fair to say that it is a historical SI base unit that is retained because of thermometers and general usage. It still can't be defined only in terms of base units (which is the technical definition of a derived unit) and that pesky &quot;degrees&quot; keeps you from using with the SI prefixes (which is part of the technical definition of an SI unit).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>but since I think we fundamentally agree more then disagree on how units should be approached for SCP Foundation fiction, I won't worry the point more then I already have.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yes absolutely! I am a total pedant and tend to get lost in the weeds. Yes, <em>technically</em> degrees Fahrenheit are just as metric as degrees Celsius and <em>technically</em> degrees Celsius fails to meet the definition of an SI unit anymore, but in common use the latter is part of the &quot;metric system&quot; and the former is not. I do think that the difference between US Customary and Imperial is important (it is actually significant for many measurements) and I would rather people learn not to confuse them.</p>
<p>TL;DR: Use either K or °C and not both. Never use °F, °De, or °R.</p>
</div>
