<p>If a broken object is made to work as intended, it's probably easier to research than if it's broken.<br />
If they risk destroying an SCP object, someone would have to evaluate the risks and the potential information that trying to fix it could yield. If they understand how it works to some degree, a site director is probably good enough. If they don't understand it very well at all, then it's probably not going to fly to eff with it for the risk of breaking it further (&quot;secure contain <em>protect</em>&quot; and whatnot).<br />
I figured it would be O5 command's job to evaluate what to do with it in that case.<br />
Of course, maybe I'm wrong.</p>
